A||||11||crzycanadian||Big Troubles!||||1||
Z||000000||crzycanadian||04-02-2001||10:29 PM||||Hey there.   On the way to work today I was comming up to a 4-way stop, when I had the clutch half way in something let go and all of a sudden the clutch petal had no pressure on it.  I had to power shift to 3rd gear from a roll, but when it found the gear I heard scraping and metal sounds.     <P>Is this a clutch problem or a transmission problem?   anyone had this happen before.  I thought it was weird.  It let go where it wasn't under any load at all.  Its a 4 speed munchie in an 86GT if that helps any.<P>If you guys have any thoughts on what it could be it would be much appreciated.<P>Thanks<BR>Levi<P>------------------<BR>86 GT 4 speed<BR>85 SC 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000001||crzycanadian||04-02-2001||10:31 PM||||By the way, when the car is in neutral and I rev it alittle bit it vibrates and doesn't sound very good.   Maybe that helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||04-02-2001||10:32 PM||||Broken clutch fork?||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||04-03-2001||03:08 PM||||Doesn't sound good.  First see if the clutch pedal is still connected to the push rod of the clutch master cylinder.  Then check to make sure the slave cylinder is still mounted; bracket hasn't broken off the transaxle, and the pieces are in place so the slave cylinder will still operate the clutch fork shaft.<P>If it's none of the above, then it's clutch time, at least.  When you take the transaxle out, you'll be able to see if the fork is broken.  Plan on some downtime.  ||||reg||9
Z||000004||rogergarrison||04-03-2001||03:23 PM||||same thing happened to me a couple summers ago. the older clutch fork is made up from a bunch of seperate pieces all welded together. mine had fell apart. new replacment is 1 pc forged. You also need new T.O. bearing and the shaft is different too. Make sure you lube the shaft good before installing it. Mines an 86 4 spd too.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||04-03-2001||03:45 PM||||NAPA has them in stock here in ATL... they are about $80 with the replacement bronze bushings.<P>check <A HREF="http://www.napaonline.com" TARGET=_blank>www.napaonline.com</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||04-03-2001||04:18 PM||||Because of the vibration I would say it could be a broken pressure plate too. Don't run it anymore. Those loose parts could break something else.||||reg||1
Z||000007||crzycanadian||04-03-2001||09:23 PM||||thanks for the help guys<P>its in the dealershit getting repaired now, just got it towed there, still don't know what the damage is<P>Thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000008||crzycanadian||04-04-2001||11:28 PM||||Well this was something they've never seen before, they opened the inspection plate and pulled my clutch out in 5 pieces, somehow it just disenegrated...  kinks odd how it even drove affter this happening.   <P>Hope this doesn't happen to anyone else, I told them to fix it and it'll be costing me $980 after taxes.<P>Later!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||04-05-2001||09:49 AM||||OUCH!<P>Hey, while they're in there, how much extra would it cost to install a new input bearing and sleeve?  That seems to be a weak link in the design, and if it breaks, it takes your clutch with it.  That happened to both mine and LZeitgeist's Formula 5-speeds.  Don't know if the 4-speed is the same, but you might want to check, since it's gonna be apart anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||04-05-2001||12:29 PM||||while its opened up, even if its good get the new forged fork. the welded up will break sooner or later and youll have to do it all over again.||||reg||1
Z||000011||crzycanadian||04-06-2001||12:09 AM||||More bad news, they got the clutch all back together and it seems there is no pressure in the hydraulic system, either my master or slave clutch cylinder is toast.  They think this is what led to my clutch failure but who knows, all I know is its going to cost an extra $500...<P>I didn't get the fork replaced, I should have but I didn't think of it at the time, hopefully mine lasts for awhile yet cause I don't think I can afford much more car troubles for awhile<P>Later!<P>------------------<BR>86 GT 4 speed<BR>85 SC 5 speed||||reg||1
